WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:54.753
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:55.023 --> 00:57.631
(Happy Anding)

3
00:58.984 --> 01:00.193
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

4
01:00.194 --> 01:01.323
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

5
01:01.324 --> 01:02.553
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

6
01:02.554 --> 01:03.664
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

7
01:06.834 --> 01:08.664
Most of my childhood memories consist of...

8
01:09.564 --> 01:12.004
the clanking of metal, my dad's heavy breathing,

9
01:12.904 --> 01:17.504
and the laughter from the TV that covered it all up.

10
01:19.044 --> 01:22.144
For that eccentric kid who loved comedy shows more than toys,

11
01:24.244 --> 01:27.654
a life-altering incident would occur a few years later.

12
01:28.784 --> 01:31.024
Rather, it was bound to happen.

13
01:34.224 --> 01:35.954
Wishing our incoming freshmen...

14
01:36.294 --> 01:39.824
endless growth and glorious achievements,

15
01:40.794 --> 01:41.864
I ask you,

16
01:42.794 --> 01:45.004
as students of the prestigious Hwaseo High,

17
01:45.364 --> 01:48.004
to uphold our noble spirit and educational philosophy...

18
01:48.374 --> 01:50.544
and spread them to the world...

19
01:50.744 --> 01:53.204
- with immense pride and dignity. - What's with...

20
01:53.274 --> 01:54.274
I sincerely hope for your commitment.

21
01:54.344 --> 01:55.374
that pitiful face?

22
01:55.444 --> 01:58.084
Lastly, I ask you once more to lead the way...

23
01:58.384 --> 02:00.083
toward an even brighter and prouder future...

24
02:00.084 --> 02:01.214
- for our prestigious Hwaseo High. - What's with the tacky fit...

25
02:01.284 --> 02:02.684
of his pants?

26
02:03.184 --> 02:04.654
That face is a tough sell.

27
02:05.254 --> 02:06.584
Thank you.

28
02:07.224 --> 02:10.564
I'd like to offer my heartfelt congratulations on your admission.

29
02:13.224 --> 02:16.064
Next, representing the incoming freshmen,

30
02:16.334 --> 02:18.403
Han Jun Seo from Class 3...

31
02:18.404 --> 02:21.004
- will read the freshman pledge. - That's him, right?

32
02:21.404 --> 02:23.544
The son of the director of Yechan Hospital.

33
02:23.804 --> 02:25.344
Born with a silver spoon?

34
02:25.644 --> 02:26.714
Pledge.

35
02:27.114 --> 02:30.084
As of today, Han Jun Seo and 192 incoming freshmen...

36
02:30.484 --> 02:32.114
have been admitted to Hwaseo High School.

37
02:32.244 --> 02:35.384
We'll abide by school regulations, elevate the school's honour,

38
02:35.454 --> 02:36.884
and, following the spirit of Hwaseo,

39
02:37.024 --> 02:39.554
in carrying on and developing our school's traditions,

40
02:39.654 --> 02:41.494
we solemnly pledge...

41
02:41.694 --> 02:43.024
to take the lead and fulfill our responsibilities.

42
02:43.524 --> 02:44.764
March 3, 2008...

43
02:45.364 --> 02:47.464
Freshman representative, Han Jun Seo.

44
02:50.864 --> 02:54.034
Seriously, he's funnier than most comedians.

45
02:54.104 --> 02:56.174
- Totally. - You're exaggerating.

46
02:57.044 --> 02:59.404
- I'm telling you, he's insane. - Hey, do it one more time.

47
02:59.474 --> 03:00.874
What, do you think I just do whatever you ask,

48
03:00.944 --> 03:02.144
just like this?

49
03:02.974 --> 03:04.244
That's Kim Nam Il from Class 5, right?

50
03:04.384 --> 03:07.214
- I heard he's a total nutjob. - He's hilarious, though.

51
03:10.084 --> 03:11.124
The absolute best.

52
03:11.524 --> 03:13.554
- I don't like him much. - Not funny at all.

53
03:15.524 --> 03:17.724
That's not how you deliver it.

54
03:18.394 --> 03:19.624
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

55
03:23.134 --> 03:24.134
Wrong.

56
03:24.704 --> 03:26.264
Hey, it goes like this.

57
03:26.904 --> 03:28.134
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

58
03:28.874 --> 03:29.904
Wrong.

59
03:30.374 --> 03:31.874
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

60
03:32.974 --> 03:34.644
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

61
03:34.714 --> 03:35.714
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

62
03:35.774 --> 03:38.644
- Good morning. - All right, page 44.

63
03:40.554 --> 03:41.854
Those seats are empty. What's going on?

64
03:48.094 --> 03:49.654
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

65
03:49.754 --> 03:50.824
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

66
03:50.894 --> 03:52.064
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

67
03:56.764 --> 03:58.404
Wrap it up and get out here.

68
04:01.374 --> 04:02.374
Holy crap.

69
04:05.544 --> 04:06.914
Hey, I just saw a snake.

70
04:07.544 --> 04:09.614
Geez, quit being dramatic and just do it.

71
04:12.544 --> 04:15.954
Freshman class rep. What are you doing?

72
04:16.084 --> 04:18.654
See, this is why you really can't judge a book by its cover.

73
04:19.284 --> 04:21.494
Hey, your dad was on TV and said, you know,

74
04:21.694 --> 04:23.664
that smoking puts holes in your bones.

75
04:23.724 --> 04:25.064
So what do you think you're doing?

76
04:25.394 --> 04:27.064
His dad is on TV? Is he an actor?

77
04:27.834 --> 04:28.834
You seriously don't know?

78
04:28.894 --> 04:30.634
You know that show every Sunday morning,

79
04:30.804 --> 04:32.064
something like "Era of Great Doctors"?

80
04:32.304 --> 04:34.404
The famous doctor on it is his dad.

81
04:34.604 --> 04:37.544
Your grandfather is a doctor, your dad is a doctor,

82
04:37.674 --> 04:40.103
and your brother goes to Hankuk Med, right?

83
04:40.104 --> 04:41.173
What does it matter if he is?

84
04:41.174 --> 04:42.774
Why do you care so much about other people's business?

85
04:42.844 --> 04:44.844
I don't care. Everyone else does.

86
04:48.014 --> 04:49.854
What are you doing? Come out so we can clean.

87
04:55.094 --> 04:58.064
Hey, you really should quit smoking.

88
04:58.324 --> 05:00.634
How heartbroken would your dad be if he found out?

89
05:07.304 --> 05:08.304
What?

90
05:09.804 --> 05:10.804
What do you want?

91
05:14.874 --> 05:16.344
Your parents must be even more heartbroken.

92
05:19.344 --> 05:20.384
What did you just say?

93
05:22.214 --> 05:23.254
You little punk.

94
05:24.154 --> 05:25.254
Take it outside.

95
05:28.794 --> 05:30.424
- You piece of... - You bastard.

96
05:30.524 --> 05:33.934
- I told you to take it outside. - Hey...

97
05:33.994 --> 05:35.194
I got crap on my hands.

98
05:36.594 --> 05:40.274
- You jerk. - Freeze!

99
05:44.904 --> 05:45.944
You crazy bastard.

100
05:46.804 --> 05:48.014
Sir, his knees are touching the floor.

101
05:48.074 --> 05:49.614
No, they're not. Not at all, sir.

102
05:49.914 --> 05:51.014
- Hold that position properly. - Yes, sir.

103
05:51.844 --> 05:54.513
Starting today, until graduation, you three are on bathroom duty.

104
05:54.514 --> 05:55.514
Got it?

105
05:55.515 --> 05:57.084
- What? - Sir.

106
05:57.324 --> 05:59.284
That seems a bit unfair, sir.

107
05:59.754 --> 06:00.824
Excuse me, Mr. Jung.

108
06:01.494 --> 06:02.494
Yes?

109
06:10.194 --> 06:11.634
Here are the sign-ups for the broadcasting festival.

110
06:12.464 --> 06:15.074
Did a lot of people sign up?

111
06:15.174 --> 06:16.234
- What's his deal? - No.

112
06:16.304 --> 06:17.603
- Why is he looking like that? - What should we do?

113
06:17.604 --> 06:19.474
The vice principal said that if we're short again this year,

114
06:19.604 --> 06:21.774
he'll cancel the festival.

115
06:26.584 --> 06:27.614
Get up, you three.

116
06:33.924 --> 06:35.424
You perform at the broadcasting festival.

117
06:35.554 --> 06:37.164
Then I'll let you off bathroom duty.

118
06:37.424 --> 06:38.424
What?

119
06:38.724 --> 06:41.394
- I don't want to embarrass myself. - I'll just clean.

120
06:43.634 --> 06:44.634
We'll do it.

121
06:47.874 --> 06:48.874
We'll perform.

122
06:49.504 --> 06:50.544
We'll do it, sir.

123
06:53.814 --> 06:55.174
Don't worry about a thing.

124
07:07.594 --> 07:09.194
I mean, I went ahead and agreed,

125
07:09.294 --> 07:10.724
but what are the three of us supposed to do?

126
07:11.494 --> 07:13.124
Hey, can you dance?

127
07:13.424 --> 07:15.164
- No. - Can you sing?

128
07:15.334 --> 07:17.834
- I'm terrible. - What are you even good at?

129
07:18.434 --> 07:19.864
- Studying. - Darn it.

130
07:24.344 --> 07:25.374
Let's do comedy.

131
07:26.244 --> 07:27.244
Comedy?

132
07:27.614 --> 07:28.974
If we just take how our teachers act...

133
07:29.044 --> 07:30.884
and do quick impressions, the kids will love it.

134
07:33.284 --> 07:34.454
That doesn't sound bad.

135
07:34.984 --> 07:35.984
Whatever.

136
07:36.414 --> 07:38.484
All right. It's settled then.

137
07:39.154 --> 07:41.524
Okay, push all the desks back.

138
07:46.194 --> 07:50.764
(The 12th Broadcasting Festival: Moonlight Paradise)

139
07:50.934 --> 07:53.064
(Green Room)

140
07:56.674 --> 07:58.643
That was an amazing performance.

141
07:58.644 --> 08:00.573
- Let's give them a big hand again. - Aren't you nervous?

142
08:00.574 --> 08:02.774
No, I've been on stages much bigger than this.

143
08:03.744 --> 08:05.444
When I won the Math Olympiad award,

144
08:05.544 --> 08:07.354
that stage was about three times this size.

145
08:07.414 --> 08:09.014
Right, good for you.

146
08:09.284 --> 08:10.424
Three times bigger, my foot.

147
08:10.484 --> 08:12.554
Now that we know him, he's the biggest nutjob.

148
08:12.624 --> 08:13.654
Thanks.

149
08:14.124 --> 08:15.293
Next up is a comedy sketch...

150
08:15.294 --> 08:16.623
prepared by Kang Tae Gu from Class 2,

151
08:16.624 --> 08:20.464
Kim Nam Il from Class 5, and Han Jun Seo from Class 3.

152
08:21.534 --> 08:22.764
Hey, wait...

153
08:25.704 --> 08:26.904
Come on, that's so childish.

154
08:28.304 --> 08:29.334
Hey, hurry up, let's go.

155
08:31.274 --> 08:35.474
One, two, three. Let's go.

156
08:35.674 --> 08:39.744
- Nam Il... - Hey, wait...

157
08:41.254 --> 08:42.684
Lastly...

158
08:46.454 --> 08:49.054
- Don't say "lastly". - Lastly...

159
08:50.464 --> 08:53.624
Freeze!

160
09:00.204 --> 09:01.204
Lastly...

161
09:12.744 --> 09:14.054
It was a crude performance.

162
09:17.454 --> 09:19.884
The makeup, the acting...

163
09:21.994 --> 09:23.124
Everything was a mess.

164
09:24.894 --> 09:26.364
On an old, creaky,

165
09:27.164 --> 09:29.094
tiny 33m² stage.

166
09:52.954 --> 09:55.824
(The 12th Broadcasting Festival: Moonlight Paradise)

167
10:07.704 --> 10:10.844
I felt something.

168
10:15.274 --> 10:17.213
Let's hear it for these three friends...

169
10:17.214 --> 10:18.613
who brought us so much laughter.

170
10:18.614 --> 10:21.554
Let's give them another big round of applause, please.

171
11:31.084 --> 11:32.084
They laughed.

172
11:36.194 --> 11:37.194
The kids...

173
11:39.364 --> 11:42.064
They were laughing at us.

174
12:11.094 --> 12:13.224
They laughed. They laughed at us.

175
12:14.134 --> 12:16.734
(Audition Ticket: Kang Tae Gu)

176
12:16.794 --> 12:19.534
(Audition Ticket: Kim Nam Il)

177
12:19.604 --> 12:22.274
(Audition Ticket: Han Jun Seo)

178
12:33.544 --> 12:37.724
(Long Live Comedy)

179
12:45.364 --> 12:50.334
(Episode 1: Ten Years Already)

180
12:50.394 --> 12:51.404
How full is it?

181
12:51.604 --> 12:53.504
I don't know. It's too dark to tell.

182
12:54.404 --> 12:57.234
I'm not even asking for a full house, just half.

183
13:00.504 --> 13:02.114
Whatever you imagine,

184
13:02.444 --> 13:04.214
you'll see so much more.

185
13:04.814 --> 13:07.684
Introducing Korea's top comedy trio.

186
13:08.454 --> 13:09.484
A.

187
13:10.084 --> 13:11.384
Su.

188
13:12.354 --> 13:15.324
Ra!

189
13:18.864 --> 13:20.834
- Hello. We're here... - To turn your minds...

190
13:20.894 --> 13:21.894
into total chaos.

191
13:22.094 --> 13:23.464
- We're Asura! - We're Asura!

192
13:29.504 --> 13:32.544
Turn off the lights. I can't sleep...

193
13:45.084 --> 13:47.353
If you're drunk, you should go home.

194
13:47.354 --> 13:49.694
If you hit it off, get a room.

195
13:49.794 --> 13:53.294
Why come to someone else's theater and make out like that?

196
13:53.394 --> 13:55.093
Stop talking and work on the ending.

197
13:55.094 --> 13:56.194
Don't we have a sketch review tomorrow?

198
13:56.864 --> 13:58.404
I already worked it out.

199
13:59.804 --> 14:02.434
- Watch this. I told you... - You always jump straight...

200
14:02.504 --> 14:03.674
into dancing, with no brain at all.

201
14:03.874 --> 14:05.344
You care about getting gigs more than being funny.

202
14:05.404 --> 14:06.504
Think I don't know?

203
14:06.574 --> 14:08.513
- Don't you want to make money? - Oh, give me a break.

204
14:08.514 --> 14:10.114
That's why you'll never make it, man.

205
14:10.214 --> 14:12.284
If I don't make it, neither do you, you idiot.

206
14:12.344 --> 14:14.414
You've got a point there, man. I'll try harder, man.

207
14:14.484 --> 14:16.654
- Hey, what are you writing? - You never know.

208
14:17.014 --> 14:18.084
Just jotting it all down.

209
14:18.154 --> 14:20.324
You psycho. Give it here.

210
14:20.384 --> 14:22.454
- Let go. Hey. - Hey, let go of my hand.

211
14:22.824 --> 14:25.794
Hey, how about this? That couple just gave me an idea...

212
14:26.294 --> 14:28.434
- Slapstick. - About time for some slapstick.

213
14:28.694 --> 14:30.964
It's the Joseon era, a noble newlywed couple.

214
14:31.104 --> 14:32.104
Good setup.

215
14:32.204 --> 14:34.503
On their wedding night, the bride gets shy,

216
14:34.504 --> 14:35.734
so he tries to blow out the candle, but it won't go out.

217
14:36.034 --> 14:38.043
- Then what? - He has to blow it out somehow.

218
14:38.044 --> 14:40.673
Right. But then the bride loses her patience,

219
14:40.674 --> 14:42.514
shoves the groom aside, and then...

220
14:46.984 --> 14:48.884
Lifts her skirt like this.

221
14:57.864 --> 14:59.224
- Trash it. - Trash it.

222
15:00.864 --> 15:03.364
- Why? I think it's funny. - Your sense of humour sucks.

223
15:03.494 --> 15:06.434
Jun Seo, name just one skit you pushed that actually did well.

224
15:14.274 --> 15:16.614
- She glared at us again. - Why is she glaring?

225
15:16.674 --> 15:19.813
- It's almost closing time. - Well, she could just come tell us.

226
15:19.814 --> 15:21.283
Why does she always give us dirty looks?

227
15:21.284 --> 15:23.554
Jun Seo, you go this way. Hey, let's head this way.

228
15:24.354 --> 15:25.384
The ice...

229
15:26.824 --> 15:29.094
Walking on eggshells around my boss by day,

230
15:29.394 --> 15:31.224
and around a cafe barista by night.

231
15:32.064 --> 15:34.164
How did my life end up like this?

232
15:34.734 --> 15:37.604
Hey, listen. What if three obnoxious customers...

233
15:37.734 --> 15:39.934
Knock it off already. Let's just take a break.

234
15:40.034 --> 15:41.434
We'll be writing more at home anyway.

235
15:41.904 --> 15:43.603
Why are you complaining before you even hear it?

236
15:43.604 --> 15:44.974
What if it's not about comedy?

237
15:46.044 --> 15:47.044
It's not?

238
15:49.814 --> 15:50.884
How did you know?

239
15:51.484 --> 15:53.944
I really can't stand him.

240
15:54.014 --> 15:56.084
I hate him more than that barista back there.

241
15:57.724 --> 15:58.784
Still, she's kind of cute.

242
16:01.809 --> 16:02.909
Smells good.

243
16:03.979 --> 16:05.049
Looks delicious.

244
16:05.909 --> 16:07.619
(Asura)

245
16:07.779 --> 16:10.119
You're doing it wrong, man. Give it here.

246
16:10.379 --> 16:11.519
Let me show you.

247
16:11.849 --> 16:15.319
Grab it tight right here, okay? Stretch it out, then pull back.

248
16:15.459 --> 16:16.589
Hey, look right here.

249
16:17.389 --> 16:19.428
Look at my lats popping. See that?

250
16:19.429 --> 16:20.799
Hey, wait, what are you wearing?

251
16:21.459 --> 16:23.398
What do you mean? It's my lats. Check it out.

252
16:23.399 --> 16:25.029
What's this? Aren't these my boxers?

253
16:26.229 --> 16:27.239
Take them off.

254
16:27.299 --> 16:28.438
There's no "yours" or "mine" in this house.

255
16:28.439 --> 16:29.439
Don't you wear mine?

256
16:29.440 --> 16:31.309
Those match Na Yeon's, you lunatic. Take them off.

257
16:31.509 --> 16:32.969
- Chill. - Take them off, you punk.

258
16:33.039 --> 16:34.239
I've known her for years, too.

259
16:34.339 --> 16:35.409
I said take them off. Go take them off.

260
16:35.479 --> 16:36.609
We're close enough for this, aren't we?

261
16:36.679 --> 16:38.009
Hey, you punk, I'm going to smash your head in.

262
16:38.079 --> 16:39.449
Hey. Take them off. Take them off right now.

263
16:39.509 --> 16:40.578
Then go bring me another pair, jerk.

264
16:40.579 --> 16:43.018
- Take them off, seriously. - No way, they're so pretty.

265
16:43.019 --> 16:44.019
Time to eat.

266
16:44.549 --> 16:45.619
Take them off after you eat.

267
16:45.689 --> 16:47.359
I might actually smash your head in.

268
16:47.419 --> 16:48.458
Why be so stingy?

269
16:48.459 --> 16:49.789
Yes, chicken skewers.

270
16:49.859 --> 16:50.859
Looks good.

271
16:52.129 --> 16:54.729
The last customers last night were wasted and left all of this behind.

272
16:55.699 --> 16:56.699
Lucky us.

273
16:57.499 --> 16:58.598
Wait, so this is...

274
16:58.599 --> 17:01.339
Food-poisoning salmonella is vulnerable to heat,

275
17:01.469 --> 17:04.268
so heating it above 75 degrees for over a minute kills it all.

276
17:04.269 --> 17:05.309
It won't kill you.

277
17:05.569 --> 17:07.069
- It won't? - Nope.

278
17:07.139 --> 17:08.139
- Hey, Jun Seo. - What?

279
17:09.209 --> 17:11.208
Saving money is great, but come on...

280
17:11.209 --> 17:12.948
Last month's maintenance fee was 78 dollars,

281
17:12.949 --> 17:14.619
and the gas was 84 dollars.

282
17:14.679 --> 17:15.679
Compared to last month, that's...

283
17:15.749 --> 17:16.979
- It's delicious. - Thanks for the food.

284
17:17.049 --> 17:19.288
- It tastes good anyway. - While we're on the subject,

285
17:19.289 --> 17:21.119
I think we're going through daily essentials way too fast.

286
17:21.189 --> 17:22.719
The toilet paper in the bathroom is completely gone.

287
17:22.819 --> 17:25.029
I told you, right? Just two wraps each time.

288
17:26.359 --> 17:28.459
This is three wraps. This is two.

289
17:29.499 --> 17:31.969
The paper dissolves way too fast for that.

290
17:32.269 --> 17:33.828
Hey, I'm not asking for three-ply.

291
17:33.829 --> 17:35.669
Can't we just buy something a little thicker?

292
17:37.169 --> 17:38.169
I'll consider it.

293
17:38.239 --> 17:40.068
- Thank you, Your Highness. - Thank you so much.

294
17:40.069 --> 17:41.539
(Make Frugality a Habit)

295
17:41.609 --> 17:42.878
That was a big decision.

296
17:42.879 --> 17:44.979
When did they put that up?

297
17:45.409 --> 17:46.409
Should I take it down?

298
17:47.419 --> 17:48.679
No, leave it.

299
17:49.219 --> 17:50.579
Never helpful in life, honestly...

300
17:51.249 --> 17:53.049
And on top of that, they put it up crooked.

301
17:54.519 --> 17:55.558
By the way...

302
17:55.559 --> 17:58.059
Why don't those guys do YouTube like the other comedians?

303
17:58.129 --> 18:00.529
They do. It's just nobody watches.

304
18:00.699 --> 18:03.059
Because they only post clips of their stage performances.

305
18:03.429 --> 18:05.499
Or videos of themselves rehearsing backstage.

306
18:05.699 --> 18:06.899
Who watches that kind of stuff?

307
18:08.099 --> 18:11.239
They could do pranks or alter egos.

308
18:13.409 --> 18:15.909
Leave them be. They say they love the stage.

309
18:16.409 --> 18:17.909
Live on the stage,

310
18:18.479 --> 18:20.009
die on the stage.

311
18:21.619 --> 18:23.419
They've got to live the way they want.

312
18:23.549 --> 18:24.549
Still...

313
18:25.549 --> 18:27.219
Those boys just don't have that killer instinct.

314
18:27.489 --> 18:28.819
They're fools, absolute fools.

315
18:30.519 --> 18:32.758
I hope today's sketch review goes well.

316
18:32.759 --> 18:34.929
I wonder how they're doing.

317
18:37.469 --> 18:39.399
- Hurry up and come out. - Hey.

318
18:39.729 --> 18:40.869
What's this?

319
18:42.899 --> 18:44.169
- What? - What's that?

320
18:46.339 --> 18:49.539
Hey, this is really expensive. Nice.

321
18:49.609 --> 18:51.379
- What's this? - Thanks for the treat.

322
18:51.449 --> 18:52.809
Hey, why are you drinking that?

323
18:52.909 --> 18:54.449
What if it was delivered to the wrong place?

324
18:54.919 --> 18:57.949
Why? Maybe someone left it for us to drink.

325
18:58.149 --> 18:59.219
Like who?

326
19:02.589 --> 19:04.089
Our fans?

327
19:13.099 --> 19:15.039
Hey, look at you. Feeling good today?

328
19:15.099 --> 19:17.269
- You're on a roll today. - He's feeling good.

329
19:18.009 --> 19:19.909
I'm drinking it. It'll spoil if we leave it here.

330
19:22.039 --> 19:25.309
- It hits right away. Good stuff. - Good?

331
19:34.859 --> 19:39.229
As expected, you can't beat natural talent.

332
19:39.289 --> 19:41.259
- So reliable. Truly. - Unbeatable.

333
19:44.399 --> 19:46.269
What's wrong? Stomachache?

334
19:46.329 --> 19:47.998
I don't know. Maybe that drink was bad.

335
19:47.999 --> 19:50.139
Serves you right for gulping it down like an idiot.

336
19:50.199 --> 19:51.739
It might just be nerves.

337
19:54.579 --> 19:56.108
- Here, a calming pill. - Oh, thanks.

338
19:56.109 --> 19:57.508
- Hey. - Thanks... What?

339
19:57.509 --> 20:00.819
Take only half. Don't space out after taking the whole thing again.

340
20:01.749 --> 20:02.919
Man, I need to use the restroom again.

341
20:02.979 --> 20:04.018
- Hey, gather around. - What?

342
20:04.019 --> 20:05.289
Gather around, come on.

343
20:08.689 --> 20:10.859
You know the drill, right? If you chicken out, you lose.

344
20:11.029 --> 20:13.158
- Don't let the crew scare you. - Okay...

345
20:13.159 --> 20:15.498
- Focus your eyes and bring energy. - Okay...

346
20:15.499 --> 20:16.899
- Got it? - Got it.

347
20:16.959 --> 20:19.329
- All right. - Hurry up. Quick. Let's go.

348
20:19.599 --> 20:21.269
- Asura! - We can do this!

349
20:21.339 --> 20:22.739
Go, go, go!

350
20:22.799 --> 20:24.739
- Come out quickly. We're late. - I'll be right there.

351
20:25.709 --> 20:29.509
Darn it... They said it would hit the daily limit today.

352
20:31.949 --> 20:34.819
- Next team. - Next team, please come in.

353
20:35.949 --> 20:37.589
- Hello. - Hello.

354
20:37.649 --> 20:39.389
- Hello. - Hello.

355
20:41.319 --> 20:43.819
Producer Park, how have you been this past week?

356
20:44.489 --> 20:45.758
Cut the crap.

357
20:45.759 --> 20:47.029
You come here weekly, so why the formality?

358
20:48.399 --> 20:50.999
Well, your well-being is the well-being of Gag Jirak.

359
20:51.199 --> 20:53.569
I always wonder if you've eaten well,

360
20:53.629 --> 20:55.169
slept well,

361
20:55.369 --> 20:56.738
or how the stocks you recently bought are doing...

362
20:56.739 --> 20:57.769
Come on...

363
21:00.569 --> 21:03.539
Enough. Stop fooling around and just start.

364
21:04.609 --> 21:05.609
Yes, sir.

365
21:09.749 --> 21:11.049
Everyone, I'm here today...

366
21:11.119 --> 21:12.849
because I heard about a primitive tribe...

367
21:12.919 --> 21:15.559
that has never been touched by modern civilization.

368
21:15.889 --> 21:20.429
So they don't feel alienated, I dressed up like a caveman.

369
21:20.629 --> 21:21.998
Do I look like one?

370
21:21.999 --> 21:23.199
(Put away the chairs after the rehearsal.)

371
21:27.299 --> 21:30.139
Yes? Perfect, you say? All right, then without further ado,

372
21:30.199 --> 21:32.309
let's go meet them.

373
21:33.509 --> 21:34.609
As we speak,

374
21:34.679 --> 21:36.339
it seems like they're making their appearance.

375
21:42.119 --> 21:43.549
They look remarkably sharp, don't they?

376
21:51.059 --> 21:52.359
Are they laughing at me?

377
22:17.079 --> 22:19.249
That concludes the new sketch reviews.

378
22:26.429 --> 22:28.059
Shoot...

379
22:28.299 --> 22:29.659
It dropped again. Seriously.

380
22:32.169 --> 22:34.269
What are you doing? Get out.

381
22:39.639 --> 22:40.639
Excuse me, sir.

382
22:40.769 --> 22:42.979
We haven't received any feedback for weeks.

383
22:43.109 --> 22:44.409
If you don't like the ending,

384
22:44.479 --> 22:46.579
- we have other versions... - It's just bad.

385
22:46.709 --> 22:47.879
It's not funny.

386
22:53.589 --> 22:55.889
You should at least tell us why,

387
22:55.959 --> 22:57.259
- so we can revise... - Hey.

388
22:58.959 --> 23:00.089
Are you lecturing me right now?

389
23:01.059 --> 23:02.299
No, that's not what I meant.

390
23:11.339 --> 23:14.309
Hey. Why have you been so hard to reach?

391
23:14.379 --> 23:15.439
Are you freezing me out?

392
23:15.609 --> 23:17.949
I heard you play golf with Producer Jang all the time.

393
23:18.009 --> 23:19.209
I know everything, okay?

394
23:19.549 --> 23:20.609
Tonight?

395
23:21.849 --> 23:24.279
I have a team dinner tonight. How about tomorrow?

396
23:27.089 --> 23:28.319
I know, right?

397
23:29.489 --> 23:31.429
I told you, I found a great place.

398
23:32.159 --> 23:33.159
Yes.

399
23:34.159 --> 23:35.599
You son of a...

400
23:37.099 --> 23:38.169
He didn't even watch it.

401
23:39.569 --> 23:40.629
My goodness.

402
23:41.899 --> 23:45.139
- Long time no see. - What's the occasion today?

403
23:45.709 --> 23:47.709
If it isn't superstar Hwang.

404
23:47.779 --> 23:49.739
My debut classmate, Hwang Chan Sung.

405
23:54.309 --> 23:56.379
Tae Gu. Long time no see.

406
23:56.619 --> 23:59.719
Why didn't you come to the reunion? Everyone wanted to see you.

407
24:00.389 --> 24:02.189
I was busy working my part-time job.

408
24:04.359 --> 24:06.459
Deliveries? Hey, isn't it...

409
24:06.529 --> 24:09.299
- tough on you? - I'm fine.

410
24:10.059 --> 24:11.069
It's kind of fun, actually.

411
24:11.129 --> 24:12.899
A comedian should be on television.

412
24:13.529 --> 24:15.499
How did your new sketch go?

413
24:17.869 --> 24:19.369
I think we have to start from scratch.

414
24:19.439 --> 24:20.809
- Did it get rejected? - Yes...

415
24:21.879 --> 24:24.009
Rejected again? Darn it.

416
24:24.279 --> 24:26.279
It's been over a year since you passed one, right?

417
24:27.919 --> 24:30.519
I mean, with you guys trying this hard,

418
24:30.719 --> 24:33.489
he could at least let you tape one. What more does he want from you?

419
24:33.989 --> 24:36.889
Bbakgu is really crossing the line, darn it.

420
24:41.829 --> 24:44.329
Should I put in a good word for you?

421
24:46.199 --> 24:47.229
Why would you?

422
24:49.639 --> 24:52.539
Don't tell me this is about you...

423
24:52.609 --> 24:54.169
ripping off my sketch back then?

424
24:54.779 --> 24:57.749
Hey, forget it. That was ages ago.

425
24:57.849 --> 24:59.449
It's fine, man. Just forget about it.

426
25:00.109 --> 25:02.319
Hey, I told you before,

427
25:02.379 --> 25:03.649
I was just watching TV by chance and...

428
25:03.719 --> 25:06.149
Well, some people...

429
25:06.219 --> 25:09.789
seem to talk behind your back, saying you only became a comedian...

430
25:09.859 --> 25:10.888
because you stole my sketch.

431
25:10.889 --> 25:13.329
Hey, does that even make sense?

432
25:13.459 --> 25:14.829
Success comes to those who are destined for it.

433
25:14.899 --> 25:16.199
Right?

434
25:19.399 --> 25:21.569
Hey, Hwang Chan Sung.

435
25:21.769 --> 25:23.439
You know we have the team dinner tonight, right?

436
25:23.499 --> 25:25.408
Make sure you come. We can't do it without the star.

437
25:25.409 --> 25:26.469
Of course, Producer Park.

438
25:26.539 --> 25:28.439
- I'll be there. - Be there, be there.

439
25:36.379 --> 25:37.649
- See you soon. - Yes, sir.

440
25:42.489 --> 25:45.729
Hey, I'd love to chat more,

441
25:46.189 --> 25:47.359
but I have to go, okay?

442
25:47.899 --> 25:50.229
You guys should come along and...

443
25:52.799 --> 25:53.869
Never mind.

444
25:54.099 --> 25:57.169
It might be a little awkward without a sketch on the air. Right?

445
25:57.569 --> 25:58.909
Take care, okay?

446
25:58.969 --> 26:00.109
See you around.

447
26:00.869 --> 26:01.979
See you.

448
26:05.979 --> 26:07.549
Not like he'd actually help.

449
26:10.679 --> 26:11.749
Hey.

450
26:12.889 --> 26:13.919
Let's go, too.

451
26:14.789 --> 26:15.789
To the team dinner.

452
26:18.329 --> 26:19.329
Hey.

453
26:20.729 --> 26:22.099
Just trust me and follow my lead.

454
26:23.499 --> 26:25.299
I'm going to butter him up properly.

455
26:28.069 --> 26:29.839
- Darn it. - Thank you.

456
26:31.069 --> 26:34.009
- Hello. - Hello.

457
26:35.639 --> 26:37.439
The standards keep dropping for that.

458
26:37.509 --> 26:39.848
- No, not at all. - He, back then,

459
26:39.849 --> 26:41.149
He was good.

460
26:41.319 --> 26:42.419
he used to do this.

461
26:45.189 --> 26:46.488
Hey, what are you saying?

462
26:46.489 --> 26:47.519
Let's go over there.

463
26:50.119 --> 26:51.659
Yes, hey, hello.

464
26:56.099 --> 26:57.599
- Excuse me, Tae Gu. - Yes?

465
26:57.659 --> 26:59.669
This table is for the Quick Service team.

466
27:00.129 --> 27:01.129
Then we'll go over here.

467
27:01.199 --> 27:04.039
That's for the Rimimiki seniors...

468
27:04.199 --> 27:07.609
- Then over there... - That's Home Ground's table...

469
27:07.669 --> 27:10.879
Then where are we supposed to sit, you punk?

470
27:13.609 --> 27:14.819
Oh, boy.

471
27:21.489 --> 27:23.989
Even if we don't have a sketch, isn't this a bit much?

472
27:24.059 --> 27:26.329
My stomach hurts. Why do I still feel so bloated?

473
27:26.389 --> 27:28.259
Sit still. How many times are you going back and forth?

474
27:28.329 --> 27:29.699
You think I want to go?

475
27:30.459 --> 27:32.199
- Hey, Tae Gu. - Yes?

476
27:32.599 --> 27:34.839
Looks like we aren't the only ones here to suck up to Bbakgu tonight.

477
27:35.769 --> 27:37.499
Everyone thinks the same way.

478
27:37.969 --> 27:40.569
How do we break through that? Let's just go.

479
27:40.639 --> 27:43.239
No way, after coming all this way, we can't just leave.

480
27:43.439 --> 27:45.309
I'm definitely getting a seat over there tonight.

481
27:47.579 --> 27:48.579
Where are you going?

482
27:50.519 --> 27:52.589
- Whose drink are you having? - What the...

483
27:52.689 --> 27:56.219
- Look who's here. Su Kyung. - Please pour me a drink.

484
27:56.289 --> 27:57.359
Sure.

485
28:12.009 --> 28:13.009
Producer Park...

486
28:14.609 --> 28:16.139
Producer Park, I bought some ice cream.

487
28:16.779 --> 28:19.948
- What did you get? - I got bars, popsicles, and cones.

488
28:19.949 --> 28:21.549
- Are you okay? - Nice.

489
28:21.619 --> 28:23.049
- You okay? - What?

490
28:24.989 --> 28:25.989
What's this?

491
28:26.349 --> 28:28.559
Kang Tae Gu, what are you doing down there?

492
28:30.819 --> 28:31.829
You scared me.

493
28:32.459 --> 28:33.459
What else?

494
28:33.659 --> 28:35.059
I came to mix you a drink, Producer Park.

495
28:35.659 --> 28:36.659
Allow me to pour you one.

496
28:37.499 --> 28:38.999
All right, pour me a glass.

497
28:39.669 --> 28:40.969
Yes, thank you.

498
28:45.509 --> 28:46.509
Okay.

499
28:51.679 --> 28:52.749
As expected.

500
28:53.279 --> 28:54.919
- Park Gu Young! - Is a real man!

501
28:54.979 --> 28:56.619
- Park Gu Young! - Is a real man!

502
28:56.679 --> 28:57.679
Applause.

503
28:57.849 --> 29:00.689
- Applause. - Stop it, stop it, stop it.

504
29:00.749 --> 29:03.389
- Hey, you're pretty good at this. - Just say the word.

505
29:03.459 --> 29:05.689
I'll mix drinks for you all night.

506
29:05.759 --> 29:08.929
Look at this brownnoser. What a total suck-up.

507
29:10.099 --> 29:11.568
By the way, Chan Sung, didn't you say...

508
29:11.569 --> 29:12.929
you had to leave early for tomorrow?

509
29:12.999 --> 29:14.939
- I did, but... - Yes?

510
29:17.069 --> 29:18.669
I think I can stay a bit longer.

511
29:19.609 --> 29:20.939
All right, sounds good then.

512
29:23.639 --> 29:25.409
Well, the more the merrier, right?

513
29:25.709 --> 29:27.679
I really love company dinner culture.

514
29:27.779 --> 29:29.948
It's only at places like this where we can have candid...

515
29:29.949 --> 29:31.689
Hey, why are your glasses empty?

516
29:31.889 --> 29:33.119
Fill them up.

517
29:33.549 --> 29:35.719
Producer Park. Let me pour yours.

518
29:37.789 --> 29:38.959
Producer Park, so about what I was saying...

519
29:39.029 --> 29:40.989
- For our sketch this time... - I'm out of cigarettes.

520
29:41.429 --> 29:42.429
Go buy me some cigarettes.

521
29:46.169 --> 29:48.039
- Excuse me? - Why, you don't want to?

522
29:48.239 --> 29:49.769
Didn't you just say something about a sketch?

523
29:52.609 --> 29:53.609
Of course I want to.

524
29:53.739 --> 29:55.409
I run the 100 meters in 12 seconds, you know.

525
29:55.839 --> 29:57.709
Start counting. Here I go.

526
29:59.409 --> 30:01.579
Man, look at that guy.

527
30:04.379 --> 30:06.649
- A pack of cigarettes, please. - Which one?

528
30:07.519 --> 30:08.858
Give me the strongest one you have. The one that will kill the fastest.

529
30:08.859 --> 30:10.389
Hurry. Here.

530
30:10.459 --> 30:13.359
- Producer Park. - Caught you red-handed, you punk.

531
30:13.889 --> 30:16.128
- Dumping your drink, are you? - I'm sorry, Producer Park.

532
30:16.129 --> 30:18.269
My stomach just happens to be really upset today.

533
30:18.329 --> 30:19.469
Cut the crap.

534
30:24.969 --> 30:26.739
Drink it. That's your punishment for slacking off.

535
30:30.679 --> 30:33.948
All right, Producer Park. I have a special talent.

536
30:33.949 --> 30:35.319
Allow me to show it to you.

537
30:44.119 --> 30:47.359
Is this punk kidding me? Seriously. Drink up.

538
30:48.329 --> 30:50.529
Producer Park, I'll drink it for him.

539
30:50.599 --> 30:51.599
Wussing out?

540
30:52.969 --> 30:54.939
You guys are no fun. Get lost.

541
30:55.199 --> 30:56.569
No, sir. Well then...

542
30:57.039 --> 30:59.569
I'll drink it in a fun way.

543
30:59.639 --> 31:00.909
That's right. You've got to drink it.

544
31:00.969 --> 31:01.979
- Bottoms up. - Yes, sir.

545
31:02.039 --> 31:05.609
- Down the hatch. - All right, clap. Applaud.

546
31:06.709 --> 31:08.479
Okay, clap, clap, clap.

547
31:08.549 --> 31:09.949
- Clap. - Bottoms up.

548
31:10.019 --> 31:11.019
Let's go.

549
31:25.699 --> 31:28.139
What's this, all of a sudden? Have you lost your mind?

550
31:29.399 --> 31:32.169
Yes. I'm about to lose it.

551
31:38.979 --> 31:40.079
So let's stop right here.

552
31:45.289 --> 31:46.289
Let's go. Get up.

553
31:48.049 --> 31:49.059
Are you getting up or not?

554
31:50.259 --> 31:51.629
Why, you little punk.

555
32:01.699 --> 32:02.898
Just because people call you "Producer"...

556
32:02.899 --> 32:04.499
you must think you're something special.

557
32:04.909 --> 32:06.638
You do know all the comedians here...

558
32:06.639 --> 32:07.939
trash-talk you behind your back, right?

559
32:08.279 --> 32:10.309
They say your comedy sense sucks, but your character sucks even more.

560
32:11.879 --> 32:13.548
- What? - I feel like crap tonight,

561
32:13.549 --> 32:14.709
so I'll be taking my leave.

562
32:17.819 --> 32:19.189
See you at the new sketch review.

563
32:25.129 --> 32:26.129
Let's go.

564
32:28.029 --> 32:29.029
Let's go.

565
32:46.679 --> 32:47.679
Hey, Kang Tae Gu.

566
32:48.179 --> 32:50.349
- Kang Tae Gu. - Producer. Sir!

567
32:50.419 --> 32:51.819
Hey, who does that punk think he is?

568
32:51.889 --> 32:53.589
Sir, that's Tae Gu.

569
32:58.446 --> 33:00.616
Tae Gu, your mouth will freeze crooked.

570
33:05.826 --> 33:09.756
What have I done? What on earth did I...

571
33:16.796 --> 33:18.266
That idiot is at it again.

572
33:20.406 --> 33:21.606
Leave him alone.

573
33:30.616 --> 33:31.646
Sit down.

574
33:32.416 --> 33:33.416
Sit.

575
33:35.016 --> 33:36.616
I told you, why did you have to butt in?

576
33:36.686 --> 33:39.226
I was handling it so smoothly all on my own.

577
33:40.626 --> 33:42.426
You already look pathetic, and watching you do that...

578
33:42.496 --> 33:43.926
pissed me off even more, all right?

579
33:44.726 --> 33:48.736
Forget it. What's done is done. It's fine.

580
33:50.466 --> 33:52.606
Yes, you're right.

581
33:55.976 --> 33:58.036
That Bbak Gu Young...

582
34:01.306 --> 34:02.316
Hey.

583
34:02.816 --> 34:04.516
When I make it big, I'm getting revenge on Bbakgu.

584
34:04.816 --> 34:06.716
I'll make sure he never sets foot in this industry again.

585
34:06.786 --> 34:08.116
Well, you know what I'll do?

586
34:08.186 --> 34:10.316
I'll keep him right by my side and slowly gaslight him...

587
34:10.386 --> 34:11.386
until he withers away and dies.

588
34:11.456 --> 34:13.626
- Sounds good. - I already took care of it.

589
34:19.996 --> 34:20.996
What's this?

590
34:22.296 --> 34:24.636
Did you seriously pack this up in all that chaos?

591
34:25.236 --> 34:26.436
It's a waste otherwise.

592
34:27.066 --> 34:28.606
Today's team dinner must have cost a fortune.

593
34:30.136 --> 34:32.176
Man. You're the scariest of all, you bastard.

594
34:32.246 --> 34:34.106
Look at you. Good job, buddy.

595
34:34.176 --> 34:35.976
- Good job, buddy. - Shoot.

596
34:37.516 --> 34:41.286
- Look at this. Here, not this one. - Shoot, what? What's this?

597
34:41.986 --> 34:43.886
- Yes. - The light turned on.

598
35:03.736 --> 35:05.906
- Are you cold? - Gosh...

599
35:06.806 --> 35:09.246
- Hold on, man. - Hey.

600
35:09.316 --> 35:12.686
- Hold still for a second. - Stop creeping me out, man.

601
35:12.746 --> 35:14.146
Today felt so long.

602
35:17.856 --> 35:18.856
Yes.

603
35:21.256 --> 35:22.996
It looks so close from here.

604
35:25.266 --> 35:28.026
Why is getting from here to there so hard?

605
35:31.396 --> 35:32.836
Back when we were starting out,

606
35:33.736 --> 35:37.476
we used to drink right here, staring up at that sign.

607
35:38.806 --> 35:39.946
We would write comedy sketches...

608
35:41.606 --> 35:43.746
and talk about what cars we would buy.

609
35:46.316 --> 35:49.416
We were completely broke back then. Just a bottle of soju and...

610
35:49.486 --> 35:51.186
- Hard candy. - Hard candy.

611
35:54.726 --> 35:57.326
It feels like yesterday, but it's already been ten years.

612
36:15.476 --> 36:16.476
You're right.

613
36:19.886 --> 36:21.446
Ten years have already passed.

614
36:38.366 --> 36:40.506
Look at him slacking off since he's almost discharged.

615
36:40.566 --> 36:42.006
Hurry your butt over here.

616
36:43.206 --> 36:44.406
Loyalty.

617
36:45.076 --> 36:48.276
Sergeant Kang Tae Gu reporting for discharge.

618
36:48.346 --> 36:50.646
- At ease. - At ease.

619
36:51.046 --> 36:52.516
- Thank you. - All right, salute.

620
36:52.586 --> 36:53.986
Look at you slacking, you punk.

621
36:54.716 --> 36:57.286
- Says the unemployed guy. Come on. - What...

622
36:57.356 --> 37:00.256
How many times must I say I'm studying for the exam, you jerk?

623
37:01.286 --> 37:04.896
He'll work at his dad's hospital once he finishes med school.

624
37:04.956 --> 37:05.966
And you?

625
37:06.126 --> 37:08.226
You're going to your dad's auto repair shop.

626
37:09.096 --> 37:11.336
What about me? What am I supposed to do?

627
37:11.736 --> 37:13.566
Are you really going to work at your dad's shop?

628
37:13.636 --> 37:16.536
That's why he majored in automotive maintenance.

629
37:16.606 --> 37:20.576
- Forget about that. Worry about me. - Just go study.

630
37:20.646 --> 37:22.816
- Studying isn't my thing. - I'm not working at the shop.

631
37:24.616 --> 37:25.616
Man.

632
37:25.686 --> 37:27.886
Spoiled talk like that ruins my buzz.

633
37:34.286 --> 37:35.596
I want to try comedy.

634
37:37.056 --> 37:38.126
For real.

635
37:39.366 --> 37:40.496
Seriously.

636
37:43.666 --> 37:44.896
What? You want to do what?

637
37:47.406 --> 37:48.636
Do you guys remember?

638
37:50.976 --> 37:52.406
Back at our broadcasting festival.

639
38:12.996 --> 38:13.996
That day,

640
38:15.496 --> 38:17.466
I can never forget that feeling.

641
38:25.576 --> 38:26.846
I have to do this.

642
38:28.146 --> 38:29.216
I want to bet my life...

643
38:30.376 --> 38:31.616
on comedy.

644
38:34.986 --> 38:36.916
Right.

645
38:37.716 --> 38:39.256
Hey, come on.

646
38:39.956 --> 38:41.856
You think you can make a living doing that?

647
38:41.926 --> 38:44.326
There are plenty of funny people out there.

648
38:44.396 --> 38:45.396
Just ten years.

649
38:46.396 --> 38:48.026
I'll give it my all for ten years,

650
38:48.736 --> 38:50.236
and if it doesn't work out, I'll quit clean.

651
38:52.036 --> 38:53.166
So...

652
39:07.086 --> 39:08.086
what do you say?

653
39:10.916 --> 39:12.126
Do you want to do it with me?

654
39:20.566 --> 39:21.726
Just for ten years.

655
39:23.466 --> 39:24.736
Just ten years.

656
39:26.436 --> 39:27.506
Let's do it together.

657
39:57.766 --> 40:01.936
To all the valued customers visiting our department store today,

658
40:02.006 --> 40:04.436
we regret to inform you...

659
40:04.606 --> 40:08.506
that the second basement level parking is currently full...

660
40:08.576 --> 40:09.846
Whoever is late today owes 1,000 dollars.

661
40:10.546 --> 40:11.546
Okay...

662
40:11.616 --> 40:15.286
Welcome, we love having you here. Yes, welcome.

663
40:15.456 --> 40:16.456
Yes.

664
40:20.256 --> 40:21.286
All right.

665
40:21.856 --> 40:25.396
My fellow Balbalta members, I think the time has come.

666
40:26.896 --> 40:29.836
Shall we head over together? Poof.

667
40:31.636 --> 40:33.606
(I'm Heading Out Now Too)

668
40:33.966 --> 40:34.966
Hey.

669
40:35.536 --> 40:37.006
- Where are you going again? - Darn it, you scared me.

670
40:37.076 --> 40:38.536
It's not even time to switch shifts yet.

671
40:38.606 --> 40:40.976
If the manager comes, tell him I went to the restroom.

672
40:41.646 --> 40:43.176
Where are you going?

673
40:43.876 --> 40:44.976
To my real job.

674
40:46.246 --> 40:48.446
Order me some hangover soup, will you?

675
40:48.816 --> 40:49.986
Stop drinking so much.

676
40:50.486 --> 40:51.486
Every single night,

677
40:51.556 --> 40:53.186
you drink and fool around with customers,

678
40:53.526 --> 40:55.596
and during the day, you just lie here like a corpse.

679
40:55.996 --> 40:58.656
My stomach. Help me.

680
40:59.766 --> 41:01.996
- What now? Does it hurt again? - My stomach...

681
41:02.796 --> 41:05.565
That's how you earn money and make a living.

682
41:05.566 --> 41:06.636
That really hurts.

683
41:07.206 --> 41:10.736
- I'm leaving now too. - It hurts. It really hurts.

684
41:10.806 --> 41:13.006
- Mr. Jung, I'm off. - Hey, tell...

685
41:13.446 --> 41:15.006
Tae Gu and Nam Il to come this weekend.

686
41:15.076 --> 41:16.416
We need to put up shelves in the storage room.

687
41:16.876 --> 41:18.945
- Okay. - Work it off with manual labour.

688
41:18.946 --> 41:20.886
- Let's go. - Let's go.

689
41:24.716 --> 41:26.656
Pepperoni with extra cheese, right?

690
41:31.896 --> 41:32.896
(Tasty Pizza)

691
41:34.826 --> 41:35.836
(Asura)

692
41:35.896 --> 41:37.136
(Kim Nam Il: Leaving Too. Got 1,000 Dollars?)

693
41:37.196 --> 41:39.606
(Leaving Now)

694
42:49.036 --> 42:50.406
(2017 QBN Open Auditions For New Comedic Actors)

695
42:50.476 --> 42:51.806
(Kang Tae Gu, Kim Nam Il, Han Jun Seo)

696
43:11.593 --> 43:13.723
The more I think about it, the madder I get.

697
43:14.263 --> 43:15.633
Can he do whatever he wants as a producer?

698
43:15.863 --> 43:18.033
Who pulls an old-school power trip like that nowadays?

699
43:18.733 --> 43:21.503
That producer is infamous for having a terrible personality.

700
43:21.563 --> 43:23.573
- Unbelievable. - He keeps telling me...

701
43:23.903 --> 43:26.473
- that I look unlikeable. - That crazy bastard!

702
43:29.813 --> 43:31.843
Babe, what if people from your company see you?

703
43:31.913 --> 43:34.083
Is he blind? I mean,

704
43:34.913 --> 43:37.013
where else in the world could you find...

705
43:37.553 --> 43:38.623
someone this adorably unlikeable?

706
43:39.423 --> 43:41.423
That's only true for you.

707
43:43.853 --> 43:46.293
- Just sit down and eat. - Na Yeon.

708
43:47.963 --> 43:48.963
Hey.

709
43:51.163 --> 43:53.263
Say hello. This is Jung Tae Hoon. We joined the company together.

710
43:54.863 --> 43:55.873
Hello.

711
43:57.133 --> 43:58.643
I'm Kim Nam Il.

712
43:58.943 --> 43:59.943
Hello.

713
44:00.243 --> 44:01.543
This is my boyfriend, Kim Nam Il.

714
44:04.043 --> 44:05.043
Na Yeon.

715
44:05.113 --> 44:06.843
That ESG portfolio I asked for earlier,

716
44:06.913 --> 44:08.313
could you send it over by today?

717
44:08.513 --> 44:10.053
Sure, I'll bring it over as soon as I can.

718
44:10.253 --> 44:13.752
How could I dare make a senior associate run back and forth?

719
44:13.753 --> 44:16.093
I'll come over to your desk.

720
44:16.923 --> 44:18.393
Senior associate?

721
44:19.363 --> 44:22.033
You didn't know? Na Yeon was promoted last month.

722
44:23.033 --> 44:24.233
Well, you see...

723
44:27.863 --> 44:30.473
Hey, your team is calling you. Go on, hurry.

724
44:32.373 --> 44:33.373
See you later.

725
44:33.443 --> 44:36.343
- Nice meeting you. - Yes, enjoy your lunch.

726
44:38.983 --> 44:41.313
Seriously, he talks way too much.

727
44:41.813 --> 44:43.853
The food got cold because of him. Let's eat quickly.

728
44:50.053 --> 44:51.323
Why didn't you tell me?

729
44:54.323 --> 44:58.393
I just forgot. It's not that big of a deal anyway.

730
45:04.703 --> 45:06.273
Yes, I guess so.

731
45:07.503 --> 45:09.413
Let's eat before lunch break ends.

732
45:09.873 --> 45:10.873
Okay.

733
45:15.383 --> 45:18.653
He kept insisting on buying me a new car.

734
45:19.083 --> 45:22.153
Ever since he switched to that big corporation,

735
45:22.223 --> 45:23.523
he's gotten way too big for his britches.

736
45:23.923 --> 45:25.593
Come to think of it,

737
45:25.663 --> 45:28.323
my son and your second one are the same age, right?

738
45:28.693 --> 45:31.663
Is he still running around trying to be a comedian or whatever?

739
45:31.793 --> 45:33.103
He wasn't funny at all.

740
45:33.233 --> 45:35.702
If he were young, I'd understand.

741
45:35.703 --> 45:37.572
With his ageing father and sick brother like this,

742
45:37.573 --> 45:40.443
he should pull himself together and act like a responsible adult.

743
45:40.503 --> 45:42.913
- Hello, sir. You're here? - Hey.

744
45:43.343 --> 45:44.913
Man, it's so hot.

745
45:45.583 --> 45:46.783
Why is it so hot today?

746
45:48.343 --> 45:50.853
- Didn't see you there, sir. - Hi, Tae Gu.

747
45:51.453 --> 45:53.353
Anyway, I'll wait at home.

748
45:53.423 --> 45:55.993
- Call me when you're done. - Sure, see you later.

749
45:57.623 --> 45:59.023
(Eunhye Auto Repair Shop)

750
45:59.593 --> 46:01.723
He complained about his knees, but he looks fine.

751
46:02.023 --> 46:03.293
What brings you here without calling?

752
46:04.163 --> 46:07.503
I came for warranty service. The back door is acting up again.

753
46:08.003 --> 46:10.973
- How on earth did you fix it? - Warranty service, my foot.

754
46:11.033 --> 46:12.143
You don't even pay for repairs.

755
46:13.643 --> 46:16.013
Dad, what are we going to do with this shameless punk?

756
46:19.543 --> 46:20.713
It's so hot.

757
46:22.853 --> 46:23.953
Get me something to drink.

758
46:24.513 --> 46:26.823
- Make it cold, with ice. - Why, you little...

759
46:27.253 --> 46:28.853
If you order your disabled brother around,

760
46:28.923 --> 46:30.223
he'll just end up doing it.

761
46:31.293 --> 46:32.563
I'll be back in a flash.

762
46:46.373 --> 46:47.843
It's so hot out in the scorching sun.

763
46:48.673 --> 46:51.213
I told you to put up a tarp here. It doesn't even cost that much.

764
46:54.883 --> 46:55.953
Need any help?

765
47:01.623 --> 47:04.593
You're trying so hard to pretend you don't hear me.

766
47:05.253 --> 47:06.263
Right?

767
47:22.273 --> 47:24.013
So, do you have some free time today?

768
47:24.143 --> 47:25.543
No, I have to go.

769
47:26.313 --> 47:27.413
I have some things to clean up.

770
47:28.883 --> 47:31.653
Dad, can you look at Tae Gu's car first?

771
47:32.823 --> 47:33.823
Please?

772
47:35.183 --> 47:36.523
He says he's busy today.

773
47:36.593 --> 47:37.953
Don't you see all the cars parked over there?

774
47:39.763 --> 47:41.863
But still...

775
47:42.193 --> 47:43.193
Forget it.

776
47:43.893 --> 47:44.933
I'll come back next time.

777
47:45.493 --> 47:46.933
Hey, Tae Gu, at least eat before you go.

778
47:48.103 --> 47:49.103
No, it's okay.

779
47:50.303 --> 47:51.333
Even if I can't be a good son,

780
47:52.033 --> 47:53.803
I should at least let Dad eat in peace.

781
47:55.573 --> 47:58.313
Dad, I'm leaving,

782
47:58.573 --> 47:59.643
so please wipe that scowl off your face.

783
48:00.283 --> 48:01.343
You'll scare the customers.

784
48:02.953 --> 48:03.953
See you, Hyun Gu.

785
48:06.153 --> 48:07.753
Come on, I told you to eat first.

786
48:09.523 --> 48:10.523
Hey!

787
48:14.663 --> 48:15.663
Seriously.

788
48:21.763 --> 48:24.103
Call Kang Tae Gu and tell him, as long as I'm here,

789
48:24.173 --> 48:26.103
don't even dream of coming to pitch a new sketch.

790
48:26.703 --> 48:30.373
He's banned from the station entirely. Got it?

791
48:30.443 --> 48:31.443
Yes, understood.

792
48:31.773 --> 48:34.013
That arrogant punk.

793
48:35.513 --> 48:36.753
How dare he mess with a producer?

794
48:37.013 --> 48:39.583
Full of fight as always, Senior Park.

795
48:40.523 --> 48:41.523
What are you doing here?

796
48:41.853 --> 48:43.753
What are you doing here? Aren't you in New York until year-end?

797
48:43.823 --> 48:46.763
Yes, I was. The director summoned me urgently.

798
48:47.463 --> 48:50.993
He's been looking for you too for a while.

799
48:51.333 --> 48:53.633
- Me? Looking for me? - Yes.

800
48:54.633 --> 48:56.903
Standards and Practices Department out of the blue?

801
48:57.233 --> 48:59.743
- That's a demotion. - Yes, it's a demotion.

802
49:01.573 --> 49:03.813
I heard you were entertained by CEO Oh again, right?

803
49:04.013 --> 49:05.813
I told you to keep your greed in check.

804
49:06.013 --> 49:08.083
- You really are unbelievable. - Entertained...

805
49:08.283 --> 49:10.883
Entertained? It was just networking.

806
49:11.113 --> 49:13.283
Can't a producer be friends with an agency CEO?

807
49:13.353 --> 49:15.023
Friends?

808
49:15.223 --> 49:16.793
So were you also close friends with the agency's rookies...

809
49:16.853 --> 49:18.453
when you were out drinking with them?

810
49:18.523 --> 49:20.623
- But... - You sure have a lot of friends.

811
49:22.023 --> 49:24.393
Just shut your mouth and pack your bags.

812
49:24.663 --> 49:25.703
Senior, please.

813
49:25.763 --> 49:27.663
You have to at least pretend to reflect on your actions...

814
49:27.703 --> 49:29.333
so that I can bring you back later.

815
49:29.873 --> 49:31.003
Just go for now.

816
49:31.733 --> 49:33.503
Then who's replacing me?

817
49:34.673 --> 49:36.373
So, while this is quite sudden,

818
49:36.673 --> 49:38.443
I've been assigned to replace Senior Park.

819
49:39.683 --> 49:40.713
I'll be blunt.

820
49:40.913 --> 49:43.283
Word of Senior Park getting fired has leaked to the press.

821
49:43.353 --> 49:44.713
People are talking all over the place.

822
49:45.113 --> 49:46.983
We need a new sketch to divert their attention.

823
49:50.653 --> 49:52.023
Put something together and bring it to me.

824
49:58.393 --> 49:59.433
Well...

825
50:00.463 --> 50:02.003
Us?

826
50:02.833 --> 50:04.472
- We'll do our best. - We'll do our best.

827
50:04.473 --> 50:05.842
- We'll give it our all. - We'll work hard.

828
50:05.843 --> 50:06.872
We'll do a great job.

829
50:06.873 --> 50:08.343
- We'll do our best. - We'll make it great.

830
50:08.403 --> 50:10.043
- We'll do our best. - We won't let you down.

831
50:21.923 --> 50:22.923
Hello.

832
50:24.423 --> 50:25.523
Let's get to it.

833
50:26.093 --> 50:28.323
Right now, every sketch takes too long to get to the punchline.

834
50:28.863 --> 50:30.333
So we should just do a bridge segment.

835
50:30.433 --> 50:34.003
Set it up openly like a talent show, and jump in between the sketches...

836
50:34.063 --> 50:36.273
to smash gourds and break wooden boards.

837
50:38.503 --> 50:39.543
Darn it.

838
50:40.343 --> 50:42.003
Feats of strength are so old school.

839
50:42.913 --> 50:46.013
Hey, why don't we go for something a little more primal?

840
50:46.883 --> 50:49.153
- Animal impressions. - That's been done to death.

841
51:02.393 --> 51:04.333
You psycho. You're embarrassing us. Stop.

842
51:05.063 --> 51:07.733
You freak, cut it out. Stop it.

843
51:31.723 --> 51:32.723
An elephant.

844
51:44.073 --> 51:46.002
- I think you're missing the point. - Sorry about this.

845
51:46.003 --> 51:47.943
- No, really. - These are the eyes, the trunk...

846
51:48.003 --> 51:49.003
See, it's an elephant.

847
51:49.073 --> 51:50.913
- No. - Where's she going?

848
51:51.043 --> 51:52.172
Just stop explaining it.

849
51:52.173 --> 51:54.313
She might laugh tomorrow, you know.

850
51:54.383 --> 51:55.582
How are you ever going to go back there...

851
51:55.583 --> 51:56.853
after humiliating yourself like that?

852
51:57.013 --> 51:59.013
Hey, that girl is the weird one.

853
51:59.583 --> 52:02.183
Whatever, forget it. Anyway, how should we end it?

854
52:02.523 --> 52:04.723
- He's just embarrassed. - Seriously.

855
52:06.523 --> 52:08.193
Or maybe instead, hey.

856
52:08.563 --> 52:10.263
Let's go visual, rely completely on visuals.

857
52:10.433 --> 52:11.933
Barefoot, let's go barefoot,

858
52:11.993 --> 52:13.233
totally lean into a wild-man concept,

859
52:13.533 --> 52:15.503
and put a pigeon on your shoulder.

860
52:16.033 --> 52:17.033
That's weak.

861
52:17.303 --> 52:19.543
- What else should we do, then? - Too weak. It's weak.

862
52:19.603 --> 52:21.203
Then put a real pigeon on him.

863
52:21.673 --> 52:23.843
Sounds great. That'll pass instantly.

864
52:23.913 --> 52:25.573
- Right. Put one on. - Okay, let's go with that.

865
52:25.643 --> 52:26.643
- Do it. - I like it.

866
52:26.713 --> 52:28.713
Go catch a pigeon. Go!

867
53:02.313 --> 53:03.513
How many times do I have to tell you?

868
53:03.583 --> 53:05.553
I'm staying in Seoul for good now.

869
53:06.123 --> 53:08.453
Should we all get together soon? Let's gather everyone up.

870
53:08.553 --> 53:10.493
Hold on, I've got another call. Don't hang up.

871
53:12.123 --> 53:13.163
Hey, Young Ju.

872
53:14.563 --> 53:15.793
Word got out already?

873
53:16.363 --> 53:19.403
Yes, I finally moved out.

874
53:20.163 --> 53:22.263
No, not by myself. I'm staying with my sister.

875
53:22.533 --> 53:23.533
Yes.

876
53:23.603 --> 53:25.533
Hey, I think my cab is here. I'll call you later.

877
53:25.603 --> 53:26.603
Taxi!

878
53:33.143 --> 53:34.143
What the...

879
53:39.053 --> 53:40.083
Guys, what's this?

880
53:40.683 --> 53:41.683
What?

881
53:42.223 --> 53:44.493
- What's this? - What?

882
53:46.193 --> 53:47.223
What's that?

883
53:51.663 --> 53:53.503
What do we do?

884
53:54.203 --> 53:56.472
What do we do? Hey, it's moving.

885
53:56.473 --> 53:58.273
Get back. It's coming out.

886
53:58.333 --> 54:00.073
- Darn it... - Hey, this... Hey.

887
54:00.143 --> 54:01.143
Hey, where are you going?

888
54:01.843 --> 54:02.843
Shoot.

889
54:06.213 --> 54:08.043
Hey, it just made eye contact with me.

890
54:09.613 --> 54:10.713
Hey.

891
54:15.853 --> 54:17.053
Call an ambulance!

892
54:17.623 --> 54:18.653
Stay back.

893
54:22.733 --> 54:25.433
(Soojung Villa, Dream Villa)

894
54:28.433 --> 54:29.433
Excuse me.

895
54:33.503 --> 54:34.543
What are you doing?

896
54:35.643 --> 54:36.673
Who are you?

897
54:46.883 --> 54:47.923
Hey, you in the black hoodie!

898
55:14.183 --> 55:16.083
Comedy has two basic rules.

899
55:16.913 --> 55:19.253
Repetition and a twist.

900
55:25.993 --> 55:26.993
Hey.

901
55:30.263 --> 55:31.963
Life follows the exact same rules.

902
55:34.133 --> 55:35.633
Hey. Who are you?

903
55:37.703 --> 55:38.903
Hey, who are you?

904
55:39.603 --> 55:40.673
Why is she so fast?

905
55:42.103 --> 55:43.113
Hey!

906
55:46.713 --> 55:47.713
Oh, no.

907
55:50.353 --> 55:51.353
(Asura)

908
55:51.413 --> 55:53.453
When the days that felt exciting just to dream...

909
55:54.853 --> 55:57.153
start to feel like a miserable loop,

910
56:08.763 --> 56:10.073
what we need right now...

911
56:19.513 --> 56:20.683
is just one plot twist.

912
57:38.323 --> 57:39.993
I'm so sorry.

913
57:43.663 --> 57:45.663
Goodness.

914
57:45.993 --> 57:50.403
- You scared me. - Do you have any drinks...

915
57:50.903 --> 57:52.203
that give you energy?

916
57:52.703 --> 57:56.942
- Give me three, please. - Three. Yes, here.

917
57:56.943 --> 57:58.413
Be careful, they're glass.

918
58:03.213 --> 58:04.253
Oh, what do I do?

919
58:05.283 --> 58:08.183
I gave her the ones I set aside because they expired.

920
58:17.093 --> 58:20.963
(Happy Anding)

921
58:24.873 --> 58:25.873
I passed.

922
58:26.603 --> 58:29.943
I passed. I really got in. I got in.

923
58:41.023 --> 58:42.053
I got accepted.

924
58:42.583 --> 58:44.053
I got the internship.

925
58:45.123 --> 58:46.863
Look. I got in, right?

926
58:47.123 --> 58:48.293
Yes.

927
58:49.993 --> 58:52.633
This was the company I really wanted to work for.

928
58:53.503 --> 58:55.333
Today is the happiest day...

929
58:55.863 --> 58:57.103
of my whole life.

930
59:03.173 --> 59:04.873
Mine too.

931
59:06.643 --> 59:08.143
Congratulations on getting the job.

932
59:10.853 --> 59:13.653
Wait. I need to call Mom.

933
59:16.253 --> 59:18.593
Mom, I got accepted.

934
59:19.963 --> 59:22.323
Where is Dad? Put him on too.

935
59:23.933 --> 59:25.693
- I just got the text. - Hey, you forgot this. Hey!

936
59:26.933 --> 59:28.663
- Take this. - Hold on.

937
59:30.473 --> 59:31.473
Thank you.

938
59:32.233 --> 59:33.343
Mom.

939
01:00:05.933 --> 01:00:07.373
Just be upfront about it.

940
01:00:07.443 --> 01:00:09.843
Tell them you're their fan and like them.

941
01:00:10.013 --> 01:00:11.643
I need to at least see her face to report her.

942
01:00:11.713 --> 01:00:12.913
Why report her?

943
01:00:13.143 --> 01:00:14.743
So I can beat the crap out of her myself.

944
01:00:15.743 --> 01:00:18.753
Hello. You're Asura, right?

945
01:00:18.853 --> 01:00:21.023
I know I've seen her somewhere...

946
01:00:21.083 --> 01:00:23.553
A crazy girl lives in this neighbourhood.

947
01:00:25.593 --> 01:00:26.793
How dare you?

948
01:00:27.323 --> 01:00:28.823
I gave that pathetic nobody a shot out of pity.

949
01:00:29.323 --> 01:00:30.593
When it's not working, it's not working.

950
01:00:30.663 --> 01:00:32.162
If we were to just quit right now,

951
01:00:32.163 --> 01:00:35.163
do you think there's anyone who would truly try to stop us?

952
01:00:35.763 --> 01:00:36.773
Nobody.

953
01:00:37.233 --> 01:00:38.703
No. If I were going to end it like this,

954
01:00:38.728 --> 01:00:39.928
I wouldn't have started.

955
01:00:40.043 --> 01:00:42.573
Here's an ambitious new segment.

956
01:00:42.803 --> 01:00:44.343
Let's go, Asura.

957
01:00:44.673 --> 01:00:45.743
- Let's go! - Let's go!
